---
import { guide, site } from "../data/site";
import ArticleLayout from "../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
	description="Project independence, development status, and the limits of demonstrations and agent-assisted workflows."
	eyebrow="PROJECT / DISCLAIMER"
	title="Disclaimer"
>
	<h2>About this website</h2>
	<p>
		SolidCraft is an independent open-source parametric CAD project. This
		website provides project information, documentation links, demonstrations,
		and links to software distributions. The current release notes and
		maintained documentation describe the software’s supported behavior and
		known limitations.
	</p>
	<p>
		This locally reviewable website is a proposed design. Production operator
		details and official-site authorization have not been established by this
		implementation.
	</p>
	<h2>Third-party names & independence</h2>
	<p>
		SolidCraft and SolidCore are independent projects. References to Autodesk,
		Fusion, NVIDIA, SMLib, and other third-party products identify workflow
		context or upstream software. They do not imply affiliation, sponsorship,
		certification, or endorsement. Third-party names and trademarks belong to
		their respective owners.
	</p>
	<h2>Development status & verification</h2>
	<p>
		The software is under active development. Features, file-format behavior,
		and supported workflows may differ between releases. Demonstrations show
		identified builds and examples; they are not a guarantee that every model or
		operation will succeed.
	</p>
	<p>
		Keep backups of important work. Independently verify dimensions, geometry,
		units, tolerances, and exported files before manufacturing or other
		consequential use. Software warranties and limitations are governed by the
		applicable licenses.
	</p>
	<p>
		The recordings on this site are screen captures of SolidCraft running the
		demonstration scripts published in its repository. The website
		implementation did not independently test those CAD or MCP sessions. Source
		review and website tests are separate from testing the application.
	</p>
	<h2>Browser storage</h2>
	<p>
		Browser-saved documents are associated with the browser and origin used by
		the application. Keep exported copies of important designs outside browser
		storage. Moving to a new website address does not automatically move
		documents saved at the previous address.
	</p>
	<p>
		The browser links in this MVP open the{" "}<a href={site.app}>
			existing upstream app
		</a
		>. Export designs before any future origin transfer, and follow the{" "}
		<a href={guide("files")}>file and storage guidance</a>. Do not clear the old
		site’s browser data before exporting important designs.
	</p>
	<h2>Agent-assisted workflows</h2>
	<p>
		Agent-assisted changes should be reviewed like other design changes.
		External AI applications and providers have their own terms and
		data-handling practices. A local MCP connection does not by itself establish
		that an external client keeps prompts, screenshots, or model information on
		the device.
	</p>
	<h2>External resources</h2>
	<p>
		External repositories, downloads, documentation, and third-party services
		operate under their own terms and policies. Software issues can be reported
		through{" "}
		<a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>the project’s GitHub issue tracker</a>.
	</p>
</ArticleLayout>
